Morgan

I'll focus my comments simply upon your query in the paragraph beginning "In addition..."

I would not present the year-specific estimates if you have used a common detection function.  Producing estimates at a level lower than the level of aggregation used in estimating the detection function results in the wrong detection function being applied to the estimates for each year.  A discussion of this can be found in Section 5.1.1 of Buckland et al. (2015:55)

By combining data across years, the interpretation of the estimates you have produced is the number of animals *on average* in the study area.

