Subject: point count data and data filter to calculate individual bird densities
Message-ID: <jFYhchtU2Og.0AuetJJCCAAJ@distance-sampling.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/distance-sampling/c/jFYhchtU2Og/m/0AuetJJCCAAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hello Distance experts,

I am experiencing some challenges with data field input and density analyses.

My project is standard point counts (10 minutes at each point), counted twice or more during each season (3 total seasons).  My study sample is well over 1000.  I had 10 count stations with two observers.  Recorded distances range from 0-250 meters. I was surveying for birds.

